4 * 18 = 72 seats in the school auditorium. One fourth of the seats were occupied by the administrators, therefore Administrators = 72 * (1/4) = 18 seats. Now, seats left over = 72 - 18 = 54 seats. One third of the seats left over were occupied by parents, therefore Parents = 54 * (1/3) = 18 seats. Seats last occupied by students = number of seats left — the number of parents = 54 - 18 = 36 seats. So, the number of students in the auditorium = 36, as calculated above.

Therefore the answer is 36

